{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogReflection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DilogReflection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogarithmArchimedeanLimit","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.SmoothSeries","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.MeanValue","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.AbelLimit","lean:module:Mathlib.NumberTheory.ZetaValues","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Asymptotics","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.NegMulLog","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Deriv","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral.FundThmCalculus"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LiTwo_eq_integral_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LiTwo_eq_integral_unit","kind":"theorem","line":443,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L443-L467","doc":"**Unit-interval integral representation**: `Li₂(y) = −∫₀¹ log(1 − yz)/z dz`\nfor `0 < y < 1`. The substitution `t = y·z` in `LiTwo_eq_integral`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LiTwo_eq_integral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LiTwo_eq_integral","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L376-L423","doc":"**Integral representation** `Li₂(x) = ∫₀ˣ −log(1-t)/t dt` for `0 < x < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LiTwo_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LiTwo_half","kind":"theorem","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L357-L363","doc":"**Special value** `Li₂(½) = π²/12 − (ln 2)²/2`, the reflection FE at\n`x = ½` (Lewin 1.16).  A clean immediate corollary of `LiTwo_reflection'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LiTwo_reflection'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LiTwo_reflection'","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L323-L355","doc":"**Brick B — the Euler reflection functional equation.**\n`Li₂(x) + Li₂(1-x) = π²/6 − log x·log(1-x)` for `0 < x < 1`.  The\nauxiliary `g = Li₂ x + Li₂(1-x) + log x·log(1-x)` is constant on `(0,1)`\n(`g' ≡ 0`), and its `x → 1⁻` boundary value is `π²/6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_log_mul_log_one_sub_nhdsWithin_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_log_mul_log_one_sub_nhdsWithin_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L271-L321","doc":"Boundary limit `log x · log(1-x) → 0` as `x → 1⁻`.  Reduce to `u = 1-x → 0⁺`\nand squeeze `|log(1-u)·log u| ≤ 2·|log u · u| → 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_LiTwo_one_sub_nhdsWithin_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_LiTwo_one_sub_nhdsWithin_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L261-L269","doc":"Boundary limit `Li₂(1-x) → 0` as `x → 1⁻` (continuity at 0 ∘ `x ↦ 1-x`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_LiTwo_nhds_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_LiTwo_nhds_zero","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L233-L259","doc":"**Continuity of the dilogarithm at 0**:  `Li₂(x) → 0` as `x → 0`.  Squeeze\nagainst `|x|/(1-|x|)` using `‖Li₂ x‖ ≤ ∑ₖ |x|ᵏ⁺¹ = |x|/(1-|x|)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_reflectionAux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_reflectionAux","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L212-L221","doc":"The reflection auxiliary `g(x) = Li₂ x + Li₂(1-x) + log x·log(1-x)` has\nzero derivative on `(0,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_log_mul_log_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_log_mul_log_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L190-L210","doc":"Derivative of `x ↦ log x · log(1-x)`:  `log(1-x)/x − log x/(1-x)` for\n`0 < x < 1` (product + chain rule). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_LiTwo_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_LiTwo_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L176-L188","doc":"Derivative of `x ↦ Li₂(1-x)`:  `log x / (1-x)` for `0 < x < 1` (chain rule\non Brick A). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_LiTwo_nhdsWithin_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_LiTwo_nhdsWithin_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L160-L174","doc":"**Abel's limit for the dilogarithm.**  `Li₂(x) → π²/6` as `x → 1⁻`.\nMathlib's `Real.tendsto_tsum_powerSeries_nhdsWithin_lt` applied to the\nBasel series `∑ 1/n² = π²/6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.LiTwo_eq_powerSeries","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LiTwo_eq_powerSeries","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L136-L158","doc":"The `LiTwo` power series in Abel-normalized form: `Li₂(x) = ∑ₙ (1/n²)·xⁿ`\n(the `n = 0` term vanishes since `1/0² = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_LiTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_LiTwo","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L70-L123","doc":"**Brick A.**  `d/dx Li₂(x) = −log(1-x)/x` for `0 < x < 1`.  Differentiates\nthe `LiTwo` power series term-by-term on a compact subinterval `(−r, r)`\nwith `x < r < 1`, where the derivative series is dominated by the summable\ngeometric series `rⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dilogDerivSeries_tsum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dilogDerivSeries_tsum","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean#L42-L54","doc":"**Brick C.**  `∑ₖ xᵏ/(k+1) = −log(1-x)/x` for `x ≠ 0`, `|x| < 1`.  Pure\nalgebra: `neg_log_one_sub_hasSum` gives `∑ xᵏ⁺¹/(k+1) = −log(1-x)`; divide\nby `x`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}